cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use corona3d in your work, please cite it, together with the model run, the coronagraph data, and the methods that it lists for each layer."
title: "corona3d: a three-dimensional reconstruction of a coronal mass ejection and the corona from public MHD, coronagraph, and radio data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aggarwal
    given-names: Keshav
    affiliation: "Space Physics Laboratory (SPL), Vikram Sarabhai Space Centre (VSSC), ISRO"
    email: keshavaggarwal2310@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-27
abstract: >-
  corona3d is a Python package that builds a three-dimensional reconstruction of a coronal mass
  ejection (CME) and the corona it propagates through, following the method described in Morosan
  et al. (2022). It draws the electron-density surface of a PSI MAS/MAST magnetohydrodynamic model
  at a chosen plasma level coloured by the Alfven speed, open and closed coronal field lines and
  the closed lines through the CME shell, the graduated cylindrical shell of the CME, the sources of
  a radio burst measured in Nancay Radioheliograph images as chains of coloured blobs at their
  Newkirk heights, and images of LASCO C2 and STEREO-B COR1 and COR2 placed in the plane of the sky
  of their spacecraft, drawn with an orthographic projection from Earth, STEREO-B, the solar north
  pole, or any chosen direction. Every layer can be switched on or off, and the default
  configuration is the CME of 2013 October 25, for which the figure follows the layout of Fig. 7 of
  Morosan et al. (2022) without reproducing it exactly.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jovian-explorer/corona3d"
url: "https://jovian-explorer.github.io/software.html#corona3d"
keywords:
  - solar corona
  - coronal mass ejections
  - MHD
  - Alfven speed
  - type II radio bursts
  - LASCO
  - STEREO
  - GCS
references:
